Usage:
    ar [-]{mrxtdpq}[uvnbail] archive file...
Commands (exactly one required):
    r           Replace or add files to the archive
    d           Delete files from the archive
    x           Extract files from the archive
    t           List a table of contents
    p           Print members to standard output
    m           Move files within the archive
    q           Quick-append files without checking for duplicates
Options:
    u           With r, replace a member only if the file is newer
    v           Verbose: trace each action (repeat to trace unchanged members)
    a           Position insert/move after the named member
    b           Position insert/move before the named member
    i           Synonym for b
    c           Suppress the "creating archive" notice
    l           Keep temporary files in the current directory, not /tmp
    n           Accepted for compatibility, ignored
    archive     The archive file to create or modify
    file...     Files/members to operate on
